WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
To know God in His many aspects is to experience Him as the “I AM.”

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:17.000
“I AM” is like a blank for us to fill in as we experience God.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:29.000
At my mother’s memorial gathering today, a sister mentioned a hymn I once taught her.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:39.000
That hymn speaks of the many aspects of Christ that we can experience.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:52.000
The hymn names forty-seven aspects, and we can experience each one.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Let us look at Psalm 23: “Jehovah is my Shepherd.”

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Jehovah means “I AM.” With Him as my Shepherd, I shall not want.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:29.000
He is everything—the Alpha and the Omega.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:37.000
If we know God only objectively and do not experience Him in daily life, we remain poor.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.000
He makes me lie down in green pastures and leads me beside waters of rest.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:59.000
A sheep lies down only when it has eaten and drunk its fill.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:10.000
God cares for our bodily needs and restores our soul.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Our soul is often confused and unsure which way to go.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:34.000
A brother who raises sheep told us that sheep have very poor eyesight.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Unable to see clearly ahead, they follow the sheep in front.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:56.000
If the sheep in front falls off a cliff, those behind may follow.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.000
That is why we need the Shepherd to lead us.
